{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0073"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c007): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c007.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0073"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/pop-rock","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/music-stage__pop-rock.g4.json","changes":[{"field":"titleEn","old":"The Stories Behind Five Stage Names","new":"The Stories Behind Six Stage Names"},{"field":"titleDe","old":"Die Geschichten hinter fünf Künstlernamen","new":"Die Geschichten hinter sechs Künstlernamen"},{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",72],["-","five"],["+","six"],["=",651],["+","**Prince.** The odd one out was born with his name: Prince Rogers Nelson (1958–2016) was named after his father's jazz trio. In 1993, locked in a dispute with his record company Warner Bros., he replaced it with an unpronounceable glyph that merges the symbols for male and female. The sign was registered under the official title Love Symbol #2, the press fell back on „The Artist Formerly Known as Prince“, and only in 2000, once the contract had run out, did he return to the name he was born with.\n\n"],["=",141],["+","\n| Love Symbol #2 | Prince Rogers Nelson | Protest against his record company |"],["=",5],["+","most of "],["=",14],["+","first "],["=",79],["+"," Prince is the exception that proves the rule: the one name chosen deliberately, as a protest, was the one nobody could say."]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",70],["-","fünf"],["+","sechs"],["=",637],["+","**Prince.** Der Sonderfall trug seinen Namen von Geburt an: Prince Rogers Nelson (1958–2016) wurde nach dem Jazztrio seines Vaters benannt. 1993, im Streit mit seiner Plattenfirma Warner Bros., ersetzte er ihn durch ein unaussprechliches Zeichen, das die Symbole für männlich und weiblich verschmilzt. Das Zeichen wurde unter dem offiziellen Titel Love Symbol #2 eingetragen, die Presse behalf sich mit „The Artist Formerly Known as Prince“, und erst 2000, als der Vertrag ausgelaufen war, kehrte er zu seinem Geburtsnamen zurück.\n\n"],["=",131],["+","\n| Love Symbol #2 | Prince Rogers Nelson | Protest gegen seine Plattenfirma |"],["=",3],["-","diese"],["+","die"],["=",1],["+","meisten dieser "],["=",14],["+","ersten "],["=",71],["+"," Prince ist die Ausnahme, die die Regel bestätigt: Der eine Name, der mit Absicht gewählt wurde, als Protest, war der, den niemand aussprechen konnte."]]}]},
